**Bug Fixed:**

The issue was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was returning `parts[1]` (the second element of the split array) instead of `parts[0]` (the first element).

**What was happening:**
- For `'hello world'`, it was returning `'world'` instead of `'hello'`
- For `'solo'`, it caused an IndexError because there's only one element at index 0

**The fix:**
Changed `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]` to correctly return the first word.

All tests now pass successfully!
